  "title": "Mobile app release process best practices: visibility, coordination, and scale",
  "summary": "For most mobile teams, release processes are set up early and rarely revisited. That is, until they start causing real pain. Missed deadlines, last-minute scrambles, and knowledge siloed in one engineer's head are all symptoms of a process that hasn't kept pace with the team as the org scales. The teams that ship consistently and confidently are the ones that treat their release process as infrastructure worth investing in.",
